          "type": "usage_note"
        },
        {
          "params": {
            "note": "SDA and SCL have internal pull-downs (0.2 uA typ, 0.4 uA max, always present) to sense disconnection. With MODE.EnSleep = 1, holding both low for tSLEEP (1.75-2.5 s) puts the IC in sleep (below 1 uA), and a rising edge on SDA or SCL wakes it. A bus that idles high does not trigger it.",
            "source": "https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/MAX17048-MAX17049.pdf (p.2 IPD and tSLEEP, p.10 Sleep Mode)"
          },
          "type": "usage_note"
        }
      ]
